            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "activity_id": 79104,
            "id": "1971951160",
            "type": "activity-reference"
          },
          {
            "activity_id": 79018,
            "id": "3889514938",
            "type": "activity-reference"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1232474038",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "didigetthis",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "activity_id": 79628,
            "id": "3744048354",
            "type": "activity-reference"
          }
        ],
        "id": "379628289",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "learnbydoing",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "It is important to realize that the autoionization equilibrium for water is established in all aqueous solutions. Adding an acid or base to water will not change the equilibrium relationship. The following example demonstrates the quantitative aspects of this connection between hydronium and hydroxide ion concentrations."
              }
            ],
            "id": "04yn4ihncbyttxs",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "739910024",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "A solution of carbon dioxide in water has a hydronium ion concentration of 2.0 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M. What is the concentration of hydroxide ion at 25 °C?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ywiec488kircm69",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We know the value of the ion-product constant for water at 25 °C:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "scz46udpohysvv7",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "betx67rbm29u51o",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "j6hd4kqu94eu4t3",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\; \\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm w}\\;=\\;\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;1.0\\times10^{-14}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We can then calculate the missing equilibrium concentration."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "7n6i9vaieaz9heh",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rearrangement of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "w"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " expression shows that [OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is inversely proportional to [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "zyrdks83ymn8ymm",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "9o0m0rw7pa5mt8s",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "mr7gkr1a6zy90zv",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\frac{K_{\\mathrm w}}{\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack}\\; =\\;\\frac{1.0\\times10^{-14}}{\\;2.0\\times10^{-6}}\\;=\\;5.0\\times10^{-9}\\;\\mathrm M",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The hydroxide ion concentration in water is reduced to 5.0 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−9"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M as the hydronium ion concentration increases to 2.0 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M. This is expected from Le Châtelier’s principle: the autoionization equilibrium reaction shifts to the left to reduce the stress of the increased hydronium ion concentration, and the hydroxide ion concentration is reduced relative to that in pure water."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "jltybr99kmj1s68",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "A check of these concentrations confirms that our arithmetic is correct:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "pcic9a6p5br3ur2",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ffr0rugh9tm900g",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tqtk73ikrnodaxh",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_\\mathrm{w}\\;=\\;\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;(2.0\\times10^{-6})(5.0\\times10^{-9})\\;=\\;1.0\\times10^{-14}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3528755144",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
